zephyr-tc32: Zephyr for the Telink TC32 (TLSR8278)

This repository is a fork of the Zephyr Project RTOS
(https://github.com/zephyrproject-rtos/zephyr), licensed under the Apache
License, Version 2.0 (LICENSE, LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt). Upstream's files and
their notices are unchanged. The whole tree is distributed under the Apache
License, Version 2.0, with the exception noted in item 3.

Added on top of upstream Zephyr v4.5.0-rc1:

1. The TC32 architecture layer: arch/tc32, the Telink SoC series
   (soc/telink/tlsr/tlsr827x), the GPIO and system timer drivers
   (drivers/gpio/gpio_b87.c, drivers/timer/telink_b87_timer.c), their
   devicetree bindings and the base of dts/tc32/telink/tlsr8278.dtsi.
   Author: Ivan Belokobylskiy (devbis), from "Zephyr for the TLSR8258 and
   Zigbee", https://github.com/devbis/zephyr-tlsr8258. Apache License 2.0.
   The files keep the headers that project gave them.

2. TLSR8278 support, the build with a mainstream clang for ARMv4T Thumb, the
   USB device controller driver, the 64-bit division and constant-divisor
   conversions, the emulator log backend, P-256 for LE Secure Connections
   (lib/crypto, the public key engine driver) and the tests under
   tests/arch/tc32 and tests/crypto (TC32.md lists them).
   Copyright (c) 2026 Go Yamamoto
   SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0

3. arch/tc32/core/softfloat: the C implementations of compiler-rt's
   floating-point builtins, unchanged from the LLVM Project
   (llvm-project llvmorg-23.1.2, compiler-rt/lib/builtins).
   Part of the LLVM Project, under the Apache License v2.0 with LLVM
   Exceptions (LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt, LICENSES/LLVM-exception.txt).

4. lib/crypto/p256-m: p256-m, the constant-time P-256 implementation as
   TF-PSA-Crypto 1.1.1 carries it, with the changes its header states for a
   build without Mbed TLS.
   Copyright The Mbed TLS Contributors. Author: Manuel Pégourié-Gonnard.
